The mailing list server is up and verified end to end.

## What's running

- **postfix** on `:25`, **mailman3** (LMTP on `127.0.0.1:8024`, plus runners and REST on `:8001`) — both started and confirmed via `mailman status` / `postfix status`.
- **List**: `reading-group@local.edu`, empty roster, ready for subscribers.

## Configuration

**`/etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg`** — `incoming: mailman.mta.postfix.LMTP`, `outgoing: deliver`, `lmtp_host: 127.0.0.1`, `smtp_host: localhost:25`, Debian paths, sqlite DB, `verp_confirmations: yes` with `verp_confirm_format: $address+$cookie`, site owner `root@local.edu`.

**`/etc/postfix/main.cf`** — `local.edu` as a local domain (so `<user>@local.edu` still lands in `/var/mail/<user>` as mbox), plus `transport_maps` sending `reading-group*@local.edu` to `lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024`. `regexp:/etc/postfix/mailman_transport.regexp` covers extended sub-addresses — the generated hash table only has bare addresses, so `reading-group-confirm+<cookie>@local.edu` (the reply address in confirmation mails) needed that fallback.

**List policies** (set, and read back to confirm they persisted): `subscription_policy=open` (no owner approval), `unsubscription_policy=confirm`, both member and non-member posting `accept`.

## Verification

`/app/eval.py` passes: direct delivery, list exists, join with confirmation. I also wrote and ran a test for the two flows the eval doesn't cover — all green:

```
OK: subscribed via both -join and -subscribe aliases
OK: list post delivered to both subscribers
OK: -leave requires confirmation and then removes bob
OK: unsubscribed user no longer receives list mail
OK: post from non-member is distributed (no owner approval)
ALL FLOWS PASS
```

Both suites were re-run green after a **full teardown** (dropped the DB, transport maps, queue) rebuilt by `/app/provision.sh` alone, and again after a mailman restart. Docs are in `/app/README-mailing-list.md`; `provision.sh` is idempotent.

## Two things worth knowing

1. **Nothing restarts the daemons on container restart** — PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, no init system. Run `/usr/local/bin/mail-services start` (also `stop`/`restart`/`status`). Postfix survives, Mailman does not; I verified the start path works from cold.
2. **Two failure modes I hit, now documented** — creating `/var/mail/<user>` as root (even empty) makes postfix refuse delivery with `Permission denied`, so mailboxes must only ever be created by delivery; and Mailman list attribute assignments in a plain script need `with mailman.database.transaction.transaction():` or they silently don't commit (my first policy pass was lost this way).

